      "title": "The Gate Was the Courthouse",
      "icon": "🏛️",
      "body": "When Wisdom cries out 'in the openings of the gates' (1:21), she's speaking at the actual civic and legal center of an Israelite town — where judges sat, deals were witnessed, and public life happened. This isn't a call to religious retreat; it's a demand to bring reverence for God into ordinary business and public life."
