  "doctrinal": "Teacher-only: 4:23's 'keep thy heart with all diligence, for out of it are the issues of life' is regularly read through a modern lens that equates 'heart' with feelings — 'guard your emotions.' I think that's a real misreading. In Hebrew thought, lev names the whole inner governing center: thought, conviction, and will together, not primarily emotion. Reading the verse as 'protect your feelings' flattens what is actually a much larger and harder command — guard what you believe, value, and decide, because everything you visibly do flows from that core. I'd correct the popular sentimental reading directly when teaching this verse rather than letting it pass.",
